        "original_id": "e1153d89-b447-5bc3-a4ef-82bf25897996",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, New South Wales Government, New South Wales Police, The Honoured Society\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia, Melbourne\n- Concepts: drug trafficking, Mafia, 'Ndrangheta\n\nFacts:\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking operated from 1977 to 1979.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking was also known as the Wodward Royal Commission.\n- The New South Wales Government initiated the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking to investigate and shut down drug trafficking in New South Wales, Australia.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking especially examined links between the New South Wales Police and the Mafia.\n- The Honoured Society is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation.\n- The Honoured Society started in Melbourne and is currently active across Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "94b13d1b-ec63-5b14-8069-7932ddb4a7c5",
        "text": "The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking (1977-1979) or Wodward Royal Commission was a royal commission initiated by the New South Wales Government to investigate and shut down drug trafficking in New South Wales, Australia, especially links between the New South Wales Police and Mafia, The Honoured Society, is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation, started in Melbourne and currently active in all of Australia.",
